export const EPILOGUE =
  "### no rows\n\naspect-ratio, container, grid, kbd, label, separator, typography, button-group, empty,\nfield (wrapper itself), calendar (day cells -- selection is instant), badge.\n\nBadge's variant colour is a prop change, not a behavioural moment -- no state machine,\nno cell. Empty appears only by its parent's choice; the parent owns that motion. These\nare exclusions by absence of behaviour, not values set to zero: a zero cell is tunable,\na missing row is a claim the moment does not exist. Contest the claim by finding the\nbehaviour, not by adding the row.\n\nTwo deliberate non-cells, recorded so they read as decisions*: enabled <-> disabled\nsnaps everywhere (state gating, not communication); alert-dialog has no close-button\nrow because a consequence-gated dialog deliberately has no casual dismiss affordance.\n\n## Consumption\n\nComponents bake the generic in source: a classes file says `duration-fast\nease-standard`, resolving to `var(--rafters-duration-fast)` etc. Studio writes the\nvalues; an intent preset is a value-set over the five namespaces. Two override planes:\n\n- **value** -- retune what `duration-fast` is (the token override system, long solid);\n- **assignment** -- move a cell off its tier: a component-declared variant where one\n  exists, or your own component source (you own it).\n\nJS-consumed cells (delays, travel, settle, presence timing) read the same\n`--rafters-*` vars through a typed runtime accessor -- one token source, two\nconsumption surfaces. No cell is ever a named token; there is one `fast`, everywhere,\nalways.\n\n## Open\n\n- DIRECTION (Sean, 2026-08-02): cell EXISTENCE should come from the behaviour layer,\n  not from this file. The behaviour contract already reserves\n  `motion?: MotionMap<Part>` (01-behavior-contract.md:125, spec-only today). When a\n  behaviour declares its motion surface, this grid's row list generates from the\n  declarations and assignments validate against them -- a cell no behaviour declares\n  and an assignment no cell backs both fail loud. This file then becomes a rendered\n  view, and matrix-vs-behaviour drift becomes structurally impossible.\n- The four non-efficient intents have no measured values; they arrive as Studio\n  presets from knobs studies, never as inventions here.\n- Whether travel distance feeds a duration suggestion for the travel cells (the #1982\n  derivation) or presets set those durations directly -- unruled; touches five rows.\n- `MOTION_COMBINATION_CONSTRAINTS` is still not an authoring gate.\n- components.md's motion column still speaks the old archetype names; retranslate to\n  point here once this file settles.\n- Onboarding must land a fresh install on efficient values, never on all-zero\n  (dead-still reads as broken). Known, sequenced later.\n";
